{
  "working": "Identify product containing named element in each reaction and determine its hybridization (d²sp³ corresponds to octahedral geometry with six-coordinate complexes). (i) N₂ + H₂ → NH₃ (or N-containing product like NH₃) which is trigonal pyramidal, hybridization sp³, not d²sp³. (ii) CuCl₂ + Cl⁻ → CuCl₂·2Cl⁻? Cu(II) typically tetrahedral or square planar, not d²sp³. (iii) CoCl₃ + NH₃ → Co(NH₃)₃Cl₃ (Co(III) ammine complex) octahedral, likely d²sp³. (iv) K⁺, Na₃Co(NO₂)₆, acetic acid → Co(III) nitrito complex, octahedral, likely d²sp³. (v) Ag + KCN + O₂ → AgCN or AgₓCNₓ? Silver cyanide likely linear or square planar, not d²sp³. (vi) Fe(CN)₂ + KCN → Fe(CN)₄²⁻ tetrahedral or square planar, not d²sp³. (vii) ZnCl₂ + NaOH → [Zn(OH)₄]²⁻ tetrahedral, not d²sp³. Thus only reactions (iii) and (iv) produce octahedral d²sp³ hybridized metal centers. Count = 2.",
  "answer": "[TYPE: chemistry] [CALC_VALUE: 2] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
  "objection": null
}

